      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "Given that $X∼U\\{5,6,7,8,9,10\\},$ compute $P(X=8).$",
      "worked_solution": "If $X$ follows a discrete uniform distribution over a set $S,$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{|S|}, & x\\in S \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $X∼U\\{5,6,7,8,9,10\\},$ and the set $S=\\{5,6,7,8,9,10\\}$ has $|S|=6$ items. So, we have\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{6}, & x=5,6,7,8,9,10 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nP(X=8)=f(8)=\\frac{1}{6}.\n$$",
